  "seoTitle": "Bekasi Mayor Tri Adhianto Questioned by Kejagung",
  "metaDescription": "The Attorney General's Office questioned Bekasi Mayor Tri Adhianto regarding a potential 2 trillion IDR state loss linked to a regional gas operational deal.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The Attorney General's Office is investigating allegations of corruption involving an oil and gas operational cooperation between local firms and Pertamina EP.",
    "Bekasi Mayor Tri Adhianto was summoned and questioned as a witness regarding the procedures used in the management of the operational contract.",
    "Advocacy groups and investigators are seeking to identify key policymakers involved in the deal, which reportedly caused state losses of 2 trillion IDR."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian Attorney General's Office (Kejagung) is conducting a formal investigation into suspected corruption within the oil and gas sector in Bekasi. The case centers on irregularities in an operational cooperation agreement (KSO) involving PT Migas Bumi Bekasi and PT Pertamina EP. Prosecutors are investigating allegations that procedural violations in the partnership resulted in state financial losses estimated at approximately 2 trillion IDR. As part of the ongoing probe, authorities have summoned several local officials, including the current Mayor of Bekasi, Tri Adhianto, and former Mayor Mochtar Mohamad. While the investigation remains ongoing, observers have urged the Attorney General's Office to expand its scope beyond the primary board of directors to uncover any policymakers who may have facilitated or authorized the contested cooperation agreements.",
